WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.259 --> 00:00:04.759
Does the Pope shit in the woods?

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:12.559
…Is a very, very rude example of a malaphor
- a mixing of two idioms with the same meaning

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:16.850
to make a brand-new idiom, usually for comedic
purposes.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.720
In this case, the original idioms are ‘Is
the Pope Catholic?’ and ‘Does a Bear Shit

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:26.470
in the Woods?’, with the answer to both
questions being a resounding ‘yes’.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:33.710
But what, I wonder, is the answer to the malaphor
these idioms create?

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:36.280
Does the Pope shit in the woods?

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.940
No, probably not.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:44.829
But then, according to the Palmarian Church,
he doesn’t relieve himself in a plush marble-lined

00:00:44.829 --> 00:00:47.520
toilet in the Vatican, either.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.370
OK, this is one of the weirder intros to a
topic I’ve ever come up with.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:56.819
So before this video is derailed completely,
maybe we should put this question to one side,

00:00:56.819 --> 00:01:04.550
just for now and start at the beginning, which,
in this case, is the Spring of 1968 near the

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:09.550
sleepy town of El Palmar de Troya in Spanish
Andalusia.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:15.050
It was 30th March, to be exact, on a stretch
of farmland where four Spanish schoolgirls

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:20.100
were picking flowers when a beautiful lady
appeared to them in a vision.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:25.880
Now, we all know that children have very active
imaginations, but the local adults decided

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.770
to take this particular bit of make-believe
seriously.

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:30.880
Why?

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:38.900
Well, Spain is, on the whole, a deeply religious
country, with around 70% of the population

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:41.470
considering themselves Catholic.

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:46.400
And if you say the words ‘visions’ and
‘beautiful lady’ to a Catholic, they’re

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:51.620
only going to come to one conclusion - the
schoolgirls had been visited by an apparition

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:54.170
of the Virgin Mary herself.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:59.330
This was understandably big news for the local
Catholics, and a large group of them flocked

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:04.180
to the site in the hope of getting themselves
a big old slice of the divine-hallucination

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:05.180
pie.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:10.869
And they were in luck - the Virgin Mary was
to show up several more times in the coming

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:17.330
weeks and months, appearing to various different
people in the area around El Palmar de Troya.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:22.909
If you’re wondering exactly what the mother
of Christ was up to wandering around the Spanish

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:28.530
countryside, intermittently revealing herself
to the local faithful, it seemed she had come

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:35.730
to deliver a message: she felt that modern
Catholicism was becoming too soft, and good

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:40.950
Catholics should return to the religion’s
earlier, stricter traditions.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:46.249
The timing of this guidance was particularly
apt, coming as it did just a few years after

00:02:46.249 --> 00:02:52.390
the conclusion of the Second Vatican Council
in 1965 - which was basically a three year

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:57.519
discussion that eventually saw the Catholic
Church relax some of its stricter rules in

00:02:57.519 --> 00:03:01.489
favour of what was considered a more progressive
approach.

00:03:01.489 --> 00:03:04.750
It was seen as a positive step forward by
many.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:10.669
But, at least according to the visions coming
out of El Palmar de Troya at the time, the

00:03:10.669 --> 00:03:13.489
Virgin Mary did not approve.

00:03:13.489 --> 00:03:19.790
One man who appeared in the Andalusian countryside
in the aftermath of these visions was a Roman

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:25.330
Catholic by the name of Clemente Domínguez
y Gómez, an insurance broker from Seville.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:31.819
If rumours are to be believed, Clemente was
known in the local Seville gay scene as la

00:03:31.819 --> 00:03:38.230
volito - the she-volt - suggesting he hadn’t
exactly been following his religion to the

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.159
letter up till that point.

00:03:40.159 --> 00:03:46.999
But all that was about to change when Clemente
had his own divine visitation - a vision of

00:03:46.999 --> 00:03:51.620
Jesus Christ and Saint Pio of Pietrelcina.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.390
This vision came a full year after Clemente
first made his pilgrimage to the site, but

00:03:56.390 --> 00:04:01.290
from that point on it seems like he really
got the hang of it, and his second vision,

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:05.209
which involved the Virgin Mary, came just
two months later.

00:04:05.209 --> 00:04:10.260
Clemente claimed these visions revealed to
him that both Freemasons and Communists were

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:16.010
in the process of infiltrating the Catholic
Church, and that the Pope at the time, Paul

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:21.270
the VI, was no longer running the show in
the Vatican, but was in fact being held hostage

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.530
by corrupt cardinals.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:29.670
It was also around this time that Clemente
reported - and very publicly displayed - stigmata,

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:35.160
wounds on his body mirroring those suffered
by Jesus during the crucifixion - bloodied

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:40.660
palms and feet, a wide gash in his side, and
even scratches on his forehead from the crown

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.490
of thorns.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:47.600
Perhaps unsurprisingly, it was at this point
the Catholic Church started to feel like things

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.810
were getting a little out of hand.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:56.040
The Archbishop of Seville came out to formally
denounce the visions in El Palmar de Troya,

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:01.260
suggesting they were a form of collective
hysteria and advising that they were not to

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.450
be taken seriously.

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:09.020
He even went so far as to forbid Roman Catholics
from visiting the area and banning all acts

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.240
of worship there.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:14.100
It’s all fun and apparitions until people
start bleeding to death.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:19.170
But the site continued to attract tens of
thousands of pilgrims both from Spain and

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:25.230
far beyond in the years that followed, during
which time Clemente successfully styled himself

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:28.460
as the principle seer of visions there.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:34.670
In 1975, following instructions he claimed
to have received in visions from both Jesus

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:40.620
and Mary - who I’m assuming by now he was
on first name terms with - Clemente Domínguez

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:49.200
y Gómez officially founded a brand-new schismatic
Catholic group called the Order of Carmelites

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.470
of the Holy Face.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:53.840
But there was one small problem.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:59.630
Clemente, remember, was an insurance broker,
which kind of undermined the validity of the

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:05.550
new austere Catholicism he was peddling – the
good old Catholics amongst you will of course

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.610
know that usury is a sin.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:13.940
But it didn’t take him long to find a solution
to this little issue in the form of Roman

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:19.020
Catholic Archbishop Ngo Dinh Thuc (no-din-toe),
older brother of the former President of South

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:24.720
Vietnam who had been assassinated in the run-up
to the Vietnam war a few years earlier.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:31.360
Convinced by the righteousness of Clemente’s
cause, Ngo Dinh Thuc officially ordained him,

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:35.150
an act that would get the Archbishop excommunicated
by the Vatican.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:08:17.360
A year later, this strange tale took a turn
for the even stranger.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:22.120
In a twist of fate so ironic it kinda makes
you wonder whether he might have found himself

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:28.900
on the wrong end of some bona fide divine
retribution, the self-styled mystical seer

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:33.190
lost his non-mystical eyesight in a car accident.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:40.370
And he wasn’t just blinded - his injuries
were so severe his eyeballs had to be removed.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:46.070
After recovering from his wounds Clemente
refused to wear eyepatches of any kind, and

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:51.710
would appear in public for the rest of his
days, empty eye sockets gazing out across

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:54.880
his congregation.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:09:00.560
A few years later on the 6th August, 1978,
Pope Paul VI died.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:05.850
It isn’t entirely clear whether Clemente
still thought the Pope was locked in a cupboard

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:10.529
as a hostage somewhere in the Vatican at this
point, but either way, it was the trigger

00:09:10.529 --> 00:09:16.880
he had been waiting for - he was finally ready
to execute his plans for religious domination.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:21.950
In a formal announcement, he explained he
was no longer to be known as Clemente Domínguez

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:29.610
y Gómez, former insurance broker from Seville,
but as Pope Gregory XVII, one true ruler not

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:36.080
just of the Order of Carmelites of the Holy
Face, but of the entire Catholic Church.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:42.990
It turned out Jesus Christ himself, along
with Saints Peter and Paul, had personally

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:48.980
popped down to crown him as Pope in yet another
handy vision.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:56.490
The Order of Carmelites of the Holy Face became
the Palmarian Church which, according to Clemente

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:04.930
- sorry, Pope Gregory XVII – had now replaced
the power and might of the Vatican and the

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:07.210
imposter pope who resided there.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:10.690
You hear that Francis you tiny old fraudster.

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:16.370
The Catholic Church took this news about as
well as you would expect, denouncing the Palmarian

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:22.670
church and its leaders, seeing it for what
it was: the blind leading the clueless – there’s

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:24.190
another malaphor for you.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:29.690
But in his new position as ‘antipope’,
Gregory XVII realised that two could play

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:30.790
at that game.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:37.890
Keen to wield his new-found popey powers,
he set about excommunicating pretty much everyone

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:39.450
he could think of.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:45.200
The actual Pope, newly appointed John Paul
II, was up first of course, and next came

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:49.790
those mischievous cardinals responsible for
all that hostage business.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:54.620
Then there was the Spanish Royal Family, all
socialists and communists, all believers of

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:57.450
false religions… you get the picture.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:11:02.680
Basically, as far as the antipope formerly
known as Clemente Domínguez y Gómez was

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:08.900
concerned, if you weren’t part of the Palmarian
Church, you could go fuck yourself.

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:15.740
Getting the hang of his new job, Gregory XVII
made himself 24 new cardinals in the space

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:22.290
of a single day, then set about making a list
of all his favourite people from history and

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.890
canonising them as saints.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:30.440
First up was Christopher Columbus - if you
want to learn more about how he didn’t quite

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:34.650
discover the New World then check out my video
on the subject, linked in the description.

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:41.430
And then came Francisco Franco, who you probably
know as General Franco, the Fascist Dictator

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:47.070
who led Spain through one of its darkest periods
between 1939 and 75.

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:52.550
There were even rumours Hitler had made the
shortlist, but it seems even antipope Gregory

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:59.300
XVII drew the line somewhere, even if that
somewhere was way, way off in the distance.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:05.830
Now, we’ve all heard plenty of stories about
fringe religious sects and strange cults that

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:11.090
get up to all sorts, from a bit of basement
buggery to the odd ritualistic murder.

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:14.660
I’ve told you about a few of them on the
channel myself.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:20.089
Most of the time these groups are led by deluded
crackpots and megalomaniacs.

00:12:20.089 --> 00:12:25.920
Outside of their followers, who are typically
lost, desperate, and vulnerable individuals,

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:29.089
they have no real power or influence.

00:12:29.089 --> 00:12:35.410
But not only did the Palmarian Church amass
several thousand followers both in Spain and

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:41.120
around the world, they also managed to get
their hands on one hell of a lot of cash while

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:42.170
they were at it.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:45.110
And I mean, a lot of cash.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:50.120
Enough to build a mini-Vatican City on the
site where the original visions of the Virgin

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.140
Mary had taken place, for starters.

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:58.660
The Cathedral-Basilica of Our Crowned Mother
of Palmar is a colossal structure complete

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:05.510
with huge domes and no fewer than eight towers,
and it’s thought to have cost upwards of

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:08.910
sixteen million euros to build.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:14.810
No expense was spared elsewhere, either - Palmarian
church cardinals and bishops deck themselves

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:20.210
out in enough bling to make P Diddy jealous,
senior members of the church get around in

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:27.100
top of the line BMWs, and the grand interior
of the cathedral looks like King Midas himself

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:32.339
came home drunk one night and crashed into
pretty much everything while looking for somewhere

00:13:32.339 --> 00:13:33.550
to throw up.

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:38.440
Truth be told, nobody knows exactly where
the cash for all these extravagances came

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:45.160
from to this day, but it’s thought the antipope
managed to secure some seriously hefty donations

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:50.620
from wealthy supporters during extensive travels
around the world.

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:54.839
Whether you’re a believer or not, you’d
probably have to admit that modern religions

00:13:54.839 --> 00:14:00.010
are, by and large, really rather welcoming
to outsiders, often doing important work in

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:04.000
the community and just generally trying to
be nice to people.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:06.500
Not so the Palmarian Church.

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:11.450
If you were to visit the Cathedral-Basilica
of Our Crowned Mother of Palmar, you would

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:17.980
not be met by a friendly church representative
offering you brochures and a cup of tea, but

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:24.980
by a five metre concrete fence barred by a
giant iron door and topped with CCTV cameras.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:28.440
Rumour has it there isn’t even a doorbell.

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:34.350
Rules within the compound are incredibly strict,
dictating what the people within can eat,

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:39.500
wear, watch, say, do, think, and feel.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:45.780
There are stories of brutal self-flagellation
and severe punishment for misdemeanours.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:50.640
Members of the Church aren’t even allowed
to talk to non-Palmarians who break any of

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:57.310
the myriad rules, and those who choose to
leave the church are immediately excommunicated.

00:14:57.310 --> 00:15:00.890
You won’t be surprised to hear that plenty
of controversy has come to light about the

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:04.370
cult - I mean ‘religion’ - over the years.

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:11.090
To name but a few we have abuse - psychological
and physical - money laundering, intimidation,

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:16.410
and even the odd mysterious death that’s
occurred behind those high walls.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:22.970
Clemente, that is, Pope Gregory XVII himself,
was accused of sexual misconduct by several

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:28.570
of his priests and nuns in the 90s - charges
which he would later admit to.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:33.790
You might think revelations like these would
be the end of a fringe sect like the Palmarians,

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:39.730
but somehow, they are still going strong,
well, maybe not strong, but they’re still

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.080
going, at least.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:48.459
When their founder and leader Antipope Gregory
XVII died in 2005, the group didn’t disintegrate

00:15:48.459 --> 00:15:50.500
as so many have before.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:57.170
No, Clemente had lined up his best mate, Manuel
Corral, to rule over the Catholic world in

00:15:57.170 --> 00:16:00.500
his stead as Pope Peter II.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:07.459
No doubt as a thank you, Antipope Peter II’s
first task was to canonise his old pal Clemente

00:16:07.459 --> 00:16:14.260
as a saint, naming him as Pope Saint Gregory
XVII the Very Great.

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:17.510
The ‘very’ was overkill if you ask me,
but hey.

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:19.360
These guys don’t do things by halves.

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:25.540
Peter II was somewhat more reserved than his
predecessor and never did claim to have any

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:27.330
divine visions.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:33.970
He did, however, bring his own brand of batshit
crazy to the job, announcing that the antichrist

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:40.480
had been born in the year 2000 and would make
his first public appearance at the age of

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:47.820
12 when he would mock Christ, before becoming
the antichrist proper at the age of 30.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:52.450
I suppose you need a bit of experience under
your belt if you’re going to take on such

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:56.110
a senior role in the destruction of all mankind.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:17:01.390
Personally, if I was going to publicly make
some grand prediction, I’d have picked something

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:07.199
a good few thousand years in the future to
eliminate any chance of looking like a wally

00:17:07.199 --> 00:17:14.799
when it didn’t come true, but I guess antipope
Peter II was just that confident on this one.

00:17:14.799 --> 00:17:20.390
Out of interest I did a quick internet search
for famous people born in the year 2000 who

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:23.559
made their first public appearance at the
age of 12.

00:17:23.559 --> 00:17:25.800
I found two possible candidates.

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:32.070
American actor Jace Lee Norman, born in March
2000 and known for playing the main character

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:38.200
in Nickelodeon’s Henry Danger - he got his
big break at age 12 in Disney Series Jessie.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:44.590
The second candidate - the Neville Longbottom
of this prophetic pair, if you will - is Samuel

00:17:44.590 --> 00:17:50.640
Sevian, a chess prodigy who became the youngest
American ever to earn the title International

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:55.250
Master at the age of 12 years and 10 months.

00:17:55.250 --> 00:18:00.960
So far as I know, neither of these two has
ever publicly dissed Christ, but it’s probably

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:03.300
worth keeping an eye on them just in case.

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:06.620
You never can be too careful when it comes
to the end of days.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:12.950
There have been two further Antipopes since
Peter II passed away back in 2011.

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:18.630
Despite coming up with an undeniably inventive
new religion, the Palmarians apparently aren’t

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.760
the most imaginative bunch when it comes to
names.

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:28.070
Peter II was followed by Gregory XVIII, and
after him came Peter III.

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:32.550
It feels a bit like one of those maths series
you used to get in school - I guess we can

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:36.710
look forward to Gregory XIX next, right?

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:43.360
Incidentally, Gregory XVIII was the first
and only Palmarian Pope so far to resign from

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:46.950
his position, rather than relinquish it on
his death.

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:49.910
The reason for hanging up his Mitre once and
for all?

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:55.950
He’d lost his faith, having come to the
startling conclusion that the Palmarian Church

00:18:55.950 --> 00:18:57.390
was one big scam.

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:59.280
Who’d have thought it.

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:05.870
Somehow, Peter III rules over all of Catholicism
to this day from his very own little Vatican

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:11.860
in El Palmar de Troya, Andalusia, and while
the number of Palmarians has dwindled over

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:17.590
the last forty years, there are a fair few
faithful who swear their allegiance to him

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.000
even now.

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:24.410
Which is why, the next time someone asks you
‘does the pope shit in the woods’, you

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:29.020
know exactly how to answer:
Which Pope?

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:36.240
Thanks for watching.

